    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p><strong>Frequency </strong>Once per day</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> You are the target of a spell you're aware of, and it has a trait that matches your selected trait from your Drachiri Benefactor.</p><hr><p><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">Your scales can reflect magic that aligns with your element, or deflect it entirely. You attempt to counteract the triggering spell, using either your spell attack modifier or a modifier equal to your class DC-10, whichever is higher. If the spell would be counteracted, it instead continues with the caster as a target instead of you. This can’t affect spells that aren’t targeted (such as area spells). Even if you fail, you gain resistance 20 to any damage you take from the spell.</span></p>"
